WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:02.969
(blues music)

00:00:04.951 --> 00:00:08.201
- [Announcer] Give it up one more time.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.543
(blues music)

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.265
- Blues is a feeling.

00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:21.387
And it is an experience.

00:00:22.715 --> 00:00:26.798
Blues is about something
that happens in my life.

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:31.195
♫ Rock me all night long

00:00:31.195 --> 00:00:33.477
My name is Beverly Watkins.

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:37.227
I was born here in
Atlanta, Georgia, in 1939.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.598
- [Narrator] Beverly Watkins was a pioneer

00:00:47.598 --> 00:00:49.550
for women in Blues.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.652
- When I was playing back in the '60s,

00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:54.756
there wasn't no female guitar players,

00:00:54.756 --> 00:00:56.006
not in Georgia.

00:01:00.089 --> 00:01:02.589
They said I played like a man,

00:01:03.673 --> 00:01:07.214
but they're using the wrong terminology.

00:01:07.214 --> 00:01:10.631
The main thing is because I play so good.

00:01:12.185 --> 00:01:13.156
- [Narrator] After high school,

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:14.468
Beverly began touring with the band

00:01:14.468 --> 00:01:16.868
Piano Red and the Meter Tones.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.425
Shortly thereafter, she was opening

00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:21.592
for some of the biggest acts in music.

00:01:24.068 --> 00:01:26.340
- We opened up for James Brown,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.173
B.B. King, Otis Redding.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.940
I played over two or 3,000 shows.

00:01:34.798 --> 00:01:38.215
Back in those days, the artists took time

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.390
and help each other.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.417
- [Narrator] Her hard classic
blues style has evolved

00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.038
over the last 60 years.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:49.017
Touring with different bands
and eventually going solo.

00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:50.894
- I never stopped.

00:01:50.894 --> 00:01:53.316
When they said I should,
I didn't pay them no mind.

00:01:53.316 --> 00:01:55.108
I kept going.

00:01:55.108 --> 00:01:59.108
Yes, it has gotten hard
out there, you know.

00:01:59.108 --> 00:02:02.358
I clean houses, I worked at car washes,

00:02:03.641 --> 00:02:07.808
I clean offices, but I never
stopped playing my music.

00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:12.729
- [Narrator] And she
has no plans on stopping

00:02:12.729 --> 00:02:14.276
anytime soon.

00:02:14.276 --> 00:02:16.110
Well into her 70s, she still puts on

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.860
a show for the crowd.

00:02:18.841 --> 00:02:22.508
- It is keeping me
living, keeping me going.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.278
I'm going to look good
and have a good time.

00:02:27.278 --> 00:02:30.111
And get up there and do my thing.

